          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.\nItems, one per line:\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:question\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Does GPU parallelism change how many of the 671 CAMELS catchments can get full Bayesian calibration instead of point optimization?\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:hypothesis\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Each catchment calibrates independently, so GPU batching turns full Bayesian treatment of all 671 into a cheap throughput problem, not a blocker.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:sequential_part\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Each catchment's posterior waits on one chain's 100,000 serial proposal-accept steps; four chains per catchment.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:method\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"none - the 671 catchments' four chains each are independent, so all 2,684 chains run side by side in one batched pass.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_lever\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"One GPU gives >=20x over CPU and finishes all 671 in under an hour, so compute is the lever here.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_not\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Vectorized CPU finishes all 671 in a couple of hours, so throughput does not decide which catchments get full Bayesian treatment.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:test_summary\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Time full Bayesian MCMC (4 chains x 1e5 iterations, R-hat<1.2) for 671 CAMELS catchments on one GPU versus a vectorized CPU and versus point optimization; measure whether GPU throughput decides how many catchments get full Bayesian treatment.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:closest_prior\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Freitas et al. 2022 GPU-optimized a hydrological model's calibration to 20x CPU speedup, on one distributed model, not batched MCMC across many GR4J catchments [s_mgb].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_mgb\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/performance-optimization-of-the-mgb-hydrological-model-for-multi-/\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:left_open\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"No published result times batched GPU MCMC giving all 671 CAMELS catchments full Bayesian GR4J treatment, so the crossover is unmeasured [s_mgb].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_mgb\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/performance-optimization-of-the-mgb-hydrological-model-for-multi-/\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:anchor\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reproduce airGR's GR4J: parameter set X=(165.05, 6.46, 422.50, 2.45) gives calibration NSE 0.495 on its example basin [s_airgr_nse].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_airgr_nse\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://hydrogr.github.io/airGR/page_3_param_sets_GR4J.html\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency criterion computed on the calibration period is better (0.495)\\\"}],\\\"value\\\":0.495}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:limits\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Shows GR4J only, not expensive distributed or hierarchical models; US CAMELS unless the optional global stretch runs; nothing about single-chain mixing limits.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s_airgr_nse\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://hydrogr.github.io/airGR/page_3_param_sets_GR4J.html\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency criterion computed on the calibration period is better (0.495)\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"anchor_nse = 0.495\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s_mgb\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/performance-optimization-of-the-mgb-hydrological-model-for-multi-/\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"speedup_threshold = 20 (PROXY)\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:camels_n\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"CAMELS US catchments\\\",\\\"value\\\":671,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"catchments\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"We present a new data set of attributes for 671 catchments in the contiguous United States (CONUS) minimally impacted by human activities.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Addor et al. 2017, HESS (CAMELS dataset)\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://hess.copernicus.org/articles/21/5293/2017/hess-21-5293-2017.html\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:dist_evals_per_catchment\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"evaluations to converge one 241-parameter distributed model\\\",\\\"value\\\":50000000,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"evaluations\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Previous results presented by Keating et al. [2010] have shown that DREAM required about 50 million surrogate model evaluations to converge to a limiting parameter distribution\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Nevada Test Site 241-parameter groundwater model (Laloy & Vrugt 2012)\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011WR010608\\\"}\n\nReturn only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"array\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"One entry per item sent, with its ref unchanged.\\\",\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"ref\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"\\\\\"card:<field>\\\\\", \\\\\"src:<source id>\\\\\", \\\\\"num:<number id>\\\\\" or \\\\\"rate:<rate id>\\\\\", as sent.\\\"},\\\"status\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"enum\\\":[\\\"SUPPORTED\\\",\\\"PARTIAL\\\",\\\"UNSUPPORTED\\\",\\\"CONTRADICTED\\\",\\\"UNREACHABLE\\\"]},\\\"page_quote\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The text on the page this status rests on.\\\"},\\\"note\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"},\\\"page_value\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"number\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"num and rate items: the value the page states.\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"ref\\\",\\\"status\\\",\\\"page_quote\\\",\\\"note\\\"]}}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"items\\\"]}\"",
